From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?=C3=98yvind=20Harboe?= <oyvind.harboe@zylin.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 13:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] dbSta: hierarchicalConnect leaves no load in the source's
 module off its hierarchical net
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

When the source and the load were in the same module, hierarchicalConnect
connected the load to the flat net only. That is right while the source
has no hierarchical net, and wrong once it has one: CTS hangs loads in
several modules off one leaf buffer, and the first load in a submodule
gives the buffer a hierarchical net in its own module, which loads in
that module connected before or after never joined. In memory the
timing graph has the flat edge; read back from the .odb, the
hierarchical view leaves those loads undriven, and every register among
them is unclocked in each later stage.

A load in the source's module now joins the source's hierarchical net,
and when hierarchicalConnect first creates that net for the source, the
loads in its module already on the flat net join it too.

Not upstreamed. Retires on the //:bump onto an OpenROAD that carries it.

Signed-off-by: Øyvind Harboe <oyvind.harboe@zylin.com>
---
diff --git a/src/dbSta/src/dbEditHierarchy.cc b/src/dbSta/src/dbEditHierarchy.cc
--- a/src/dbSta/src/dbEditHierarchy.cc
+++ b/src/dbSta/src/dbEditHierarchy.cc
@@ -418,6 +418,15 @@ void dbEditHierarchy::hierarchicalConnect(odb::dbITerm* source_pin,
                                 (Net*) source_pin_flat_net,
                                 (Net*) source_db_mod_net);
         top_source_mod_net = source_db_mod_net;
+        // Loads in this module that were connected to the flat net while
+        // the source had no hierarchical net join the new one, or the
+        // hierarchical view leaves them undriven.
+        for (odb::dbITerm* iterm : source_pin_flat_net->getITerms()) {
+          if (iterm != source_pin && iterm->getModNet() == nullptr
+              && iterm->getInst()->getModule() == lowest_common_module) {
+            iterm->connect(source_db_mod_net);
+          }
+        }
       } else {
         top_dest_mod_iterm->connect(top_source_mod_net);
       }
@@ -445,6 +454,10 @@ void dbEditHierarchy::hierarchicalConnect(odb::dbITerm* source_pin,
     // 3.8. During the addition of new ports and new wiring we may
     // leave orphaned pins, clean them up.
     cleanUnusedHierPins(source_parent_tree, dest_parent_tree);
+  } else if (source_db_mod_net && dest_pin->getModNet() != source_db_mod_net) {
+    // Same module: the dest joins the source's hierarchical net, or the
+    // hierarchical view leaves it undriven.
+    dest_pin->connect(source_db_mod_net);
   }
 
   dlogHierConnDone();
